WEBVTT

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.860
The Pokémon World Championships...

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:08.200
A trial to crown
the greatest Pokémon battler.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:14.740
In the hopes of battling Dande,
the current Supreme Monarch,

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.660
Satoshi is participating
in the Championships.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:22.960
Satoshi has defeated the formidable Saito,
and risen up to 36th place.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:26.840
Now,
who will he be facing today?

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.050
Everyone’s yellin’ for me.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.680
I’ve gotta win this!

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:27.960
Is this really
where I’m gonna battle?

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:30.130
Hmm...

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:33.840
Well, this is where
those Team Yell guys said we should go...

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:36.840
<i>We’re the thoughtful Team Yell!</i>

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.260
The thoughtful and kind Team Yell,
with a message to tell!

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:44.850
Today’s battle won’t be here
in Shoot City after all!

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:48.020
Spike Town’s the place,
for real!

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:50.730
They said that, but...

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:53.990
Oh, there’s a Gym here.

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:55.950
That must be the place.

00:02:58.160 --> 00:02:59.240
Let’s go!

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.380
Here’s a number I’ve been saving!

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:12.090
Excuse me!

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:15.170
Strinder! Discharge!

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.140
Hey, that’s dangerous!

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.980
I’m rehearsing right now.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:30.900
Nobody’s allowed in here.

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:33.650
Isn’t this supposed to be a Gym?

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.860
It is.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:38.610
This is our stage, Spike Gym.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:43.620
I’m the Gym Leader,
the Evil-type Pokémon prodigy.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:46.290
They call me the Sorrowful Nezu!

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:47.830
Let me introduce my band!

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:50.040
Backup vocals:
Tachifusaguma!

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.550
Drums:
Gorillander!

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:56.800
Guitar:
Strinder High!

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:00.220
Bass:
Strinder Low!

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.640
Strinder! Punk Pokémon!
Electric/Poison type!

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:10.690
When clawing at its chest protrusions,

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:15.610
its High Form sounds like it’s strumming a guitar;
and its Low Form, a bass guitar!

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:18.610
Concert’s in an hour.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:19.910
Come back then.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:23.910
My name is Satoshi!

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:26.790
I’m here for
a Championships battle!

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:28.920
Satoshi...

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:32.170
The one from Kanto,
in the Hyper Class?

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:34.340
Yeah! You’ve heard of me?

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.260
Ooh, Satoshi, you’re famous!

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:37.840
This is odd.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:41.640
Mary should be waiting for you
at Shoot Stadium already.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:44.060
Huh? Shoot Stadium?

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:47.480
Some “thoughtful Team Yell” guys
told us the battle was here...

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:49.440
Don’t tell me they...

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:51.350
<i>Yell!</i>

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:56.980
Those guys of ours...
I’m sorry for the trouble.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:59.450
And wait, who’s Mary?

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:00.450
My sister.

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:02.160
Your sister?

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:05.490
This isn’t good, Satoshi!

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:06.990
We don’t have time!

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:10.580
What do I do?! What do I do?!

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:13.330
What do I do, what do I do,
what do I do...?!

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:15.290
I take full responsibility.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:19.220
I’ll take you to Shoot City.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:21.970
Whoa, this is cool!

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:26.100
Satoshi, you go on ahead.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.640
We’ll catch up to you later.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:28.680
Okay!

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:31.520
Make sure to hold on tight.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:32.650
Here we go!

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.500
Um...

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:52.080
Can’t we go any faster?

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.830
My motto is “safety first.”

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:55.500
Oh...

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:59.420
Mr. Nezu,
what is Team Yell?

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:01.340
Mary’s fans.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.380
Her fans?

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:06.180
They used to be
Spike Gym’s trainers, too.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:10.810
They’ll use any trick they can think of
if it’s for Mary.

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:13.100
That’s why they lied to me?

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:16.650
Oh, but I wouldn’t mind
battling at Spike Gym!

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:20.530
Mary can’t show
her full potential there.

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:26.740
Spike Town doesn’t have
a Power Spot for Daimax.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:29.790
So you don’t use Daimax, Mr. Nezu?

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.790
Right. I like ordinary battles.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:38.380
But because of that,
the Gym doesn’t see many challengers,

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:40.380
and the town’s wound up
almost deserted.

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:44.630
The reason Mary
entered the Championships...

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:52.060
...is that she hopes that becoming Champion would
make Spike Town famous, and help revitalize it.

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:53.930
Revitalize it, huh...?

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:59.820
She wants people to think,
“Wow, even Spike Town has trainers this tough?”

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:03.240
Team Yell has the same goal.

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:07.910
But... That should be my duty,
shouldn’t it?

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.200
I’m hopeless.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:15.580
All you folks watching...
The scheduled start time has come and gone,

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:18.710
but Competitor Satoshi
has yet to show himself.

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:22.000
If he doesn’t turn up,
Competitor Mary will win by default!

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:27.760
<i>Win by default!
Win by default!</i>

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:29.760
I don’t want that!

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:34.680
I wanna ‘ave a
right and proper battle!

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.020
I’ll wait for ‘im!

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:47.110
Thank you, Mr. Nezu!

00:07:57.830 --> 00:07:59.420
Sorry I’m late!

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:07.510
Took your time.

00:08:08.510 --> 00:08:10.260
I’m so sorry about that.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:13.930
Hey! How dare you
make our girl wait so long?!

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:16.310
You’re gonna fail!

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:19.270
What?! You wanna go there
after you went and tricked me?!

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:24.280
You don’t got any right to battle!

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:26.240
Our girl’s winning by default!

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:27.700
Shut your gob!

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:32.580
Was that true?
They tricked you?

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:33.330
Yeah.

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:35.160
They said the battle was moved.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:37.960
But Mr. Nezu drove me here.

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:38.870
My bro did?

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.380
We just wanted our girl to win!

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:44.170
See, a victory for you’s
a victory for Spike Town, too!

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:45.550
Not like this, it ain’t!

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:52.300
Mr. Nezu...

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:54.310
Big bro...

00:08:55.390 --> 00:09:00.140
Mary! Give it all you’ve got
in your battle!

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:06.360
Competitor Mary’s brother Nezu, who is also
Spike Town’s Gym Leader, has arrived to cheer her on!

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:19.460
Satoshi.

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:23.580
I got skin in this game
too, y’know!

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:25.460
I can’t afford to lose this!

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.800
Mr. Nezu told me.

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:29.800
You wanna revitalize
the town, right?

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:31.340
Pretty much.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:33.890
But I’ve come a long way
to get here myself!

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:35.140
I can’t lose here!

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:37.970
Let’s hurry.

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:39.390
Everyone’s waitin’ for us.

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:41.980
Yeah.
I’m looking forward to today!

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:44.100
Thank you for waiting.

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:45.730
Now, the match begins!

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:52.030
I made it...

00:09:52.030 --> 00:09:53.820
Good job making it here.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.570
Mr. Nezu...

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:58.580
It’s all thanks to
the Armorgaw Taxi.

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:03.710
You gotta win this, Satoshi!

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:07.960
The Pokémon World Championships
Hyper Class.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:11.470
And here are the two trainers
for today’s match!

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:17.470
Currently ranked 29th, a new star hailing from
Galar’s Spike Town: Competitor Mary!

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:21.230
<i>Our girl!
You’re gonna prevail!</i>

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:23.140
Her fan club?!

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:25.440
Well, something like that.

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:30.070
Currently ranked 36th,
hailing from Kanto’s Masara Town,

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:34.700
and on a winning streak after recently defeating
Competitor Saito: Competitor Satoshi!

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:38.030
Satoshi! Go for it!

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:42.000
We can see it!
He’s gonna fall!

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:45.330
We can hear it!
He’s gonna bawl!

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:49.210
Now, today’s battle will be a 1v1.

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:52.460
All right, both sides send out
your Pokémon at the same time.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:53.220
3...

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:54.220
2...

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:55.220
1...

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:56.720
Go!

00:10:56.720 --> 00:10:59.350
Gänger! I choose you!

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:02.060
Go, Olonge!

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:13.940
Olonge! Buildup Pokémon!
Evil/Fairy type!

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:16.860
Its hairs work like muscle fibers!

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:21.080
When its hairs unfurl, they latch on to opponents,
ensnaring them as tentacles would!

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:24.330
Olonge is Mary’s ace.

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:28.790
Gänger just got
a huge power-up, too!

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:32.170
I’m counting on you, Gänger!

00:11:33.340 --> 00:11:37.720
I’ve gotta win this if I’m gonna be the Champion!
I’m comin’ at ya with everythin’ I’ve got!

00:11:56.530 --> 00:11:59.030
Battle, start!

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:01.330
Soul Crush!

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:05.160
Magical Shine!

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:16.010
Olonge swings and misses!

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:19.760
Okay! Ice Punch!

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:30.270
Let’s make this quick!
Shadow Ball!

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:34.940
Olonge! Do it!

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:42.990
Groveling Jab!

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:49.080
There’s the Groveling Jab!

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.420
That’s Olonge for you!

00:12:50.420 --> 00:12:55.170
His hair is a shape-shifting weapon!
It’s super effective!

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:56.920
Right on the mark.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:58.800
All right!

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:00.340
Wow...

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:03.050
That’s Mary and Olonge’s
special move.

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:07.060
But that’s not all Mary can do.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:11.060
I see Satoshi’s wearing
a Daimax Band, too.

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:13.610
Who’s going first?

00:13:14.190 --> 00:13:16.320
Olonge, here goes!

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:30.040
Mary used hers first!

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:34.250
My bro might not use it...
But if it helps me win...

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:35.880
Kyodaimax!

00:13:49.310 --> 00:13:50.600
So they did it.

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:53.480
<i>Kyodaimax is the best!</i>

00:13:56.190 --> 00:13:59.360
Mary specializes in Daimax battles.

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:02.030
The one thing you can’t do
at Spike Gym.

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:05.030
She has her own way of battling.

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:11.870
Me and Mary, we should just both do what we can
to revive Spike Town, each in our own way.

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:14.830
Now, faced with
Kyodaimax Olonge,

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:18.500
what will Gänger and
Competitor Satoshi do?

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:20.760
Kyodai Snooze!

00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:25.800
Magical Shine!

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:32.770
Amazing! He stopped her ultimate attack,
Kyodai Snooze, with Magical Shine!

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:34.770
Interesting.

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:37.940
Satoshi’s battles
are always crazy.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:40.070
Keep holding on!

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:53.290
Gänger!

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:56.040
Gänger’s overcome
with drowsiness!

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:01.920
But it resisted, resisted!
It is resisting!

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:06.180
Gänger!
You’re so cute! So cute!

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:09.300
Morpeko...
Is that even possible?

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:13.060
Resisting a Kyodai Snooze...

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:18.560
They might prove t’ be
at least a li’l interesting.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:21.690
Let’s go, Gänger!
Sludge Bomb!

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:29.370
Gänger’s playing with Olonge,
using the tricky moves only Ghost types can pull off!

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:31.660
Then how about this?!
Dai Earth!

00:15:39.630 --> 00:15:42.170
Gänger got caught in
the Dai Earth!

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:52.600
Gänger put its all
into a Sludge Bomb!

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:55.180
But Olonge didn’t even flinch!

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:57.600
Gänger, you okay?!

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:00.610
Now, it’s our turn!

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:03.570
He’s doing it!

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:05.990
Let’s get huge!

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:12.740
Kyodaimax!

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:28.970
Gänger also used Kyodaimax!

00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:33.560
Shoot Stadium is quaking
from this Kyodaimax showdown!

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:35.020
Perfect!

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:36.890
Dai Acid!

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:42.900
Dai Fairy!

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:01.750
Olonge turned back!

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:04.630
All right, Gänger! Dai Ice!

00:17:14.890 --> 00:17:16.810
Soul Crush!

00:17:26.610 --> 00:17:28.070
He’s strong...

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:30.780
Sorry, but the winner here’s
gonna be me!

00:17:30.780 --> 00:17:33.200
Olonge! DD Lariat!

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:39.660
Let’s go! Kyodai Phantom!

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:48.510
Even the Kyodai Phantom
can’t stop the DD Lariat!

00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:50.800
<i>Our girl!</i>

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:53.590
That’s the end of
Gänger’s Kyodaimax.

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:56.430
Olonge! Charge in!

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:00.980
In that case...

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:03.060
Gänger! Swallow Olonge!

00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:10.070
It swallowed him!

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:12.700
Is that even possible?!

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:17.280
Great work, Gänger!

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:22.000
There goes the Kyodaimax!

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:25.330
And with it, Olonge is released!

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:31.420
The way he avoided leaving himself defenseless
as the Kyodaimax wore off... Incredible!

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:33.590
That Satoshi’s quite good.

00:18:35.390 --> 00:18:36.510
Stomping Tantrum!

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:45.190
Stomping Tantrum becomes more powerful
if your last move missed.

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:48.940
Shadow Ball!

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:53.070
Go!

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:24.390
Olonge is unable to battle!
Gänger wins!

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:26.730
As such, the winner is
Competitor Satoshi!

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:31.780
And the victor of this Kyodaimax battle
is Competitor Satoshi!

00:19:31.780 --> 00:19:33.900
All right!

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:37.570
He did it!

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:45.330
Our girl!

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:48.130
We did it, Gänger!

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:53.340
Olonge.

00:19:54.590 --> 00:19:56.090
You did great.

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:05.140
Amazing!

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:08.400
Olonge! You were really cool!

00:20:11.570 --> 00:20:13.110
Based on the results of this battle,

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:17.650
the Pokémon World Championships
rankings will be updated!

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:24.040
With this victory, Competitor Satoshi
rises to 15th in the Hyper Class!

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:33.130
Your Gänger was pretty strong.

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:36.050
Your Olonge was strong, too!

00:20:36.050 --> 00:20:38.260
You kept making me sweat!

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:44.930
You’ve gotten stronger, Mary.

00:20:44.930 --> 00:20:48.690
You should let out your regrets
at our next concert.

00:20:48.690 --> 00:20:49.520
Yeah.

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:53.020
Our girl,
that was incredible!

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:59.240
All the people enthralled by our girl battling
wanna go to Spike Town now!

00:20:59.240 --> 00:21:02.240
Mr. Nezu!
This is gonna revive the town!

00:21:02.620 --> 00:21:04.870
Looks like you succeeded, Mary.

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:07.790
Come on,
give them a bigger smile.

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:09.710
Yeah.

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:20.590
Satoshi, thanks for today.

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:25.600
But don’t think
I’m givin’ up yet.

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:29.560
Let’s both do our best!

00:21:31.650 --> 00:21:36.270
Winning another battle, this time against Mary,
Satoshi’s rank continues to rise.

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:38.990
The Master Class is just up ahead!

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:09.530
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.530 --> 00:23:10.870
Go!

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:15.120
I’m gonna go train
with Mr. Dande now!

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:16.120
Mr. Dande?!

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:17.210
Why?

00:23:17.210 --> 00:23:21.800
Dande’s actually nothing
like you’d think from his public image.

00:23:21.800 --> 00:23:24.720
Mr. Dande,
do you train like this every day?!

00:23:24.720 --> 00:23:26.380
Yeah. Isn’t it fun?

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:28.260
It’s super fun!

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:30.310
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.310 --> 00:23:33.600
Up Close! Dande’s Special Training!!
